<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Feb base metals import prices up - AFTAK.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Feb base metals import prices up - AFTAK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's non-ferrous metals import prices rose in February due to gains in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Import prices of base metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(US$ a tonne CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		     Origin	   Feb	 Jan</p>
<p> Copper (99.95 pct)    Chile	   2,486     2,552</p>
<p> Copper scrap (berry)  U.S.	    2,403     2,436</p>
<p> Aluminium (99.7 pct)  Australia     1,700     1,655</p>
<p> Lead (99.99 pct)	China	     700	 764</p>
<p> Zinc (99.995 pct)     S.America     1,271     1,184</p>
<p> Nickel (99.9 pct)     Canada	  8,087     7,237</p>
<p> Tin (99.85 pct)	 Malaysia	6,033     5,931</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
